1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:07,011
Left: the booking page as Ada Alpha. Right: the booking page as Ben Bravo, in a separate browser frame. Below: a terminal.

2
00:00:07,011 --> 00:00:15,994
Both users see 10 Available items (Ada) and 10 (Ben); price $100 on Ada's screen, $100 on Ben's.

3
00:00:15,994 --> 00:00:20,499
TEST 1, same-moment hold: Ada and Ben pressed Hold on Item 1 together. Ada sees "Held" and "In your cart"; Ben sees "Someone else holds that item." and the item as "Restocking" (Hold button disabled: true).

4
00:00:20,499 --> 00:00:27,673
Ada's cart reads "Item 1, 7s left"; Ben's cart is "empty". Price is still $100 for Ada and $100 for Ben: holding does not move it.

5
00:00:27,673 --> 00:00:31,177
TEST 2, payment fails: the hold ran out and Ada pressed Pay: "No active hold: your hold ended or you have none."

6
00:00:31,177 --> 00:00:39,926
Item 1 is "Available" again for Ada and "Available" for Ben, restocked at the same price: $100 on both screens.

7
00:00:39,926 --> 00:00:47,436
TEST 3, payment succeeds: Ada holds Item 2 ("Held"). Ben sees it as "Restocking", greyed, Hold button disabled: true. Price $100.

8
00:00:47,436 --> 00:00:57,154
Ada paid: "Paid $100". The price is now $110 on Ada's screen and $110 on Ben's (0.5 s after the click). Item 2 is "Available" again.

9
00:00:57,154 --> 00:01:03,702
Ben can hold Item 2 again, now at $110: "Held", cart "Item 2, 12s left".

10
00:01:03,702 --> 00:01:12,753
Ben paid: "Paid $110" - the price he saw when he paid. The price is now $120.

11
00:01:12,753 --> 00:01:18,988
TEST 4, two payments at once: Ada holds Item 3 and Ben holds Item 4. Both carts are counting down.

12
00:01:18,988 --> 00:01:29,995
They pressed Pay at the same moment: Ada sees "Paid $120", Ben sees "Paid $130". Each was charged a different price; the price is now $140 on Ada's screen and $140 on Ben's.

13
00:01:29,995 --> 00:01:49,057
Running the real test command in the terminal: node --test on all three test files, including the browser end-to-end test file. Output streams live.

14
00:01:49,057 --> 00:02:05,061
Test run finished (exit 0): the terminal shows "tests 35", "pass 35", "fail 0" - 35 pass, 0 fail.

15
00:02:05,061 --> 00:02:12,064
Final state: Ada's and Ben's screens both show price $140; the terminal still shows "pass 35" and "fail 0".
